Looking at the verification errors, the issue is that when we recursively call `Prove(s[1..])`, we need to first establish that `K.Clean(s[1..])` holds. This requires calling `O.TailInvariant(s)` before the recursive call.

The `TailInvariant` lemma in Ops.dfy has:
- requires `K.Clean(s) && 2 <= |s|`
- ensures `K.Clean(s[1..])`

So in the `else` branch where `|s| >= 2`, we should call `O.TailInvariant(s)` first to establish `K.Clean(s[1..])`, then we can make the recursive call `Prove(s[1..])`.

```json
{
  "HelperA.dfy": "if |s| < 2 {
      O.Base(s);
    } else {
      O.TailInvariant(s);
      Prove(s[1..]);
      O.Boundary(s);
      O.Keep(s);
      assert s == [s[0]] + s[1..];
    }",
  "HelperB.dfy": "if |s| < 2 {
      O.Base(s);
    } else {
      O.TailInvariant(s);
      Prove(s[1..]);
      O.Boundary(s);
      O.Keep(s);
      assert s == [s[0]] + s[1..];
    }"
}
```

